---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../config/site.js';

const UPDATED = '10 June 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data: microphone audio is processed on-device and never uploaded, preferences stay in your browser, and there are no trackers.`}
>
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 sm:pt-14 pb-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-hover dark:text-accent-light">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink dark:text-dark-ink">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mute dark:text-dark-mute">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p>
        This privacy policy explains what happens — and what deliberately does
        not happen — when you use {SITE_NAME} (the “Service”). The short
        version: the microphone audio never leaves your device, we do not run
        advertising trackers, and the only data we keep is what your browser
        stores for you.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Microphone audio</h2>
      <p>
        When you press <strong>Start measuring</strong>, your browser requests
        microphone access and streams audio into the page using the Web Audio
        API. That stream is analysed in memory to compute a decibel reading
        and is discarded frame by frame. <strong>We do not record, store,
        transmit, or share audio.</strong> No audio file is ever created on our
        servers (we do not operate any server that could receive it), and the
        microphone stream stops as soon as you pause the meter, switch tabs,
        or leave the page.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Data stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>The Service saves a small set of preferences using your browser’s
        localStorage:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>decibel-theme</code> — light or dark appearance.</li>
        <li><code>decibel-calibration</code> — your calibration offset.</li>
        <li><code>decibel-threshold:*</code> — alarm limit per page.</li>
        <li><code>decibel-alarm:*</code> — alarm enabled state per page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data stays on your device, is never synced to us, and can be
        removed at any time by clearing site data for this domain.
      </p>

      <h2>3. What we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, names, or email addresses (unless you choose to email us).</li>
        <li>No advertising cookies or cross-site trackers.</li>
        <li>No location data, device fingerprints, or analytics profiles.</li>
        <li>No uploaded sound levels or measurement history.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider (Cloudflare Pages) processes
        standard technical request logs — IP address, user agent, requested
        URL, and timestamp — for delivery and security purposes. These logs are
        operational, retained for a short period by the provider, and are not
        used to build profiles of individual visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The Service itself sets no cookies. Preferences use localStorage
        instead, which is not sent with HTTP requests.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        We embed no third-party widgets, fonts, ads, or social pixels. The
        pages you load come from this site alone.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is suitable for classroom use and does not knowingly
        collect personal information from anyone, including children.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If the way the Service handles data ever changes, we will update this
        page and revise the date above. Continued use after a change
        constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Write to
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We answer
        every privacy inquiry.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
